  "changes": [
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/qKGcB6vZ#5sWG4uuq",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "A replay of one logical call is the same call only when it names the same checkout: the same arguments in another checkout are work for another workhorse. A delegation to a checkout whose workhorse has no thread that can run turns starts it first; the other three workhorse tools refuse a checkout with no ready workhorse, and say what a checkout is. stop_workhorses stops every running workhorse of the calling tab session through the shared workhorse operation and says what each stop observed. Tool results distinguish accepted requests from observed outcomes."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/qKGcB6vZ#ZDMIGM5P",
      "field": "responsibility",
      "value": "The frozen tool manifests and their digests: what the coordinator may ask for, the checkout each workhorse tool takes, and the whole-work Stop, which takes none and reports what it observed"
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/qKGcB6vZ#LIpURyJE",
      "field": "responsibility",
      "value": "Delegate, steer, inspect, manage pending requests, and stop all work for the workhorse of one checkout"
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/qKGcB6vZ#LIpURyJE",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Inspection reads actual turns, recent progress, descendants, and pending requests. Stop clears pending requests and interrupts the proven work tree. It observes settlement and reports complete, partial, or unconfirmed results. New work waits for resolution and a fresh user request. Existing ownership and epoch records govern effects."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/qKGcB6vZ#hxZxt8Wy",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Turn completion reports that turn only, in one sentence that names the checkout of the workhorse, which is the one argument every workhorse tool takes, and carries no identity. Whole-work Stop reports its observed result separately. Inspection supplies identities, remaining work, and recovery actions. A missing turn identity never proves success."
    },
